WEBVTT

00:04:29.755 --> 00:04:36.596
AHP: Historically, it has been defined
as a feeling of giving up,

00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:41.294
a feeling like you can't
keep going anymore.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.696
And I think that that describes
a lot of the most intense,

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.396
acute, stereotypical cases of burnout.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.801
AG: Annie's definition
tracks with how burnout

00:04:51.825 --> 00:04:53.496
has traditionally been understood.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.196
That when you burn out,
you burn all the way out.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:59.256
Recently though, all the talk of burnout

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.595
has made the definition
seem bigger and blurrier.